---
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { hubBreadcrumbs } from "../../data/tools";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const breadcrumbs = hubBreadcrumbs("fees");
---
<Layout title="Stripe, PayPal & Gumroad Fee Calculators | MathMyRate" description="Free fee calculators for Stripe, PayPal, Gumroad, and Lemon Squeezy: see what each takes from a sale and what you keep, from published pricing." ogImage="/og/fees.png" breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-10 md:px-8 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
    <h1 class="display mt-4 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-5xl">Payment Fee Calculators</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Know what a sale really pays you.</p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Fee tools are built only for documented, sourced scenarios. When a case is unsupported, the tool says so plainly instead of guessing a rate.</p>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <a href="/fees/stripe-fee-calculator/" class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-line bg-[#fafbfd] p-8 transition-transform hover:-translate-y-1"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Card processing</p><h2 class="display mt-5 text-3xl font-bold">Stripe Fee Calculator</h2><p class="mt-4 text-ink/65">US online card pricing for domestic, international, and manually entered cards: the fee, what you keep, and what to charge.</p><span class="mt-8 block font-semibold text-navy">Open calculator →</span></a>
      <a href="/fees/paypal-fee-calculator/" class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-line bg-[#fafbfd] p-8 transition-transform hover:-translate-y-1"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Wallet checkout</p><h2 class="display mt-5 text-3xl font-bold">PayPal Fee Calculator</h2><p class="mt-4 text-ink/65">PayPal Checkout, card, invoice, international, and QR code payments: the fee, what you keep, and what to charge.</p><span class="mt-8 block font-semibold text-navy">Open calculator →</span></a>
      <a href="/fees/gumroad-fee-calculator/" class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-line bg-[#fafbfd] p-8 transition-transform hover:-translate-y-1"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Digital marketplace</p><h2 class="display mt-5 text-3xl font-bold">Gumroad Fee Calculator</h2><p class="mt-4 text-ink/65">Direct sales versus Discover marketplace sales, with the documented volume threshold.</p><span class="mt-8 block font-semibold text-navy">Open calculator →</span></a>
      <a href="/fees/lemon-squeezy-fee-calculator/" class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-line bg-[#fafbfd] p-8 transition-transform hover:-translate-y-1"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Digital products</p><h2 class="display mt-5 text-3xl font-bold">Lemon Squeezy Fee Calculator</h2><p class="mt-4 text-ink/65">Order fees on the order total, including tax, for US, international, PayPal, and subscription orders.</p><span class="mt-8 block font-semibold text-navy">Open calculator →</span></a>
      <a href="/fees/stripe-vs-paypal-fees/" class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-line bg-[#fafbfd] p-8 transition-transform hover:-translate-y-1"><p class="eyebrow">Compare / Payments</p><h2 class="display mt-5 text-3xl font-bold">Stripe vs PayPal Fees</h2><p class="mt-4 text-ink/65">Price the same sale under Stripe's and PayPal's published US rates, side by side.</p><span class="mt-8 block font-semibold text-navy">Compare fees →</span></a>
      <a href="/fees/gumroad-vs-lemon-squeezy-fees/" class="rounded-[1.5rem] border border-line bg-[#fafbfd] p-8 transition-transform hover:-translate-y-1"><p class="eyebrow">Compare / Digital products</p><h2 class="display mt-5 text-3xl font-bold">Gumroad vs Lemon Squeezy Fees</h2><p class="mt-4 text-ink/65">See what each platform keeps from the same digital product sale.</p><span class="mt-8 block font-semibold text-navy">Compare fees →</span></a>
    </div>
    <section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl border-t border-line pt-10"><h2 class="display text-3xl font-bold">Sourced scenarios only</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Each fee tool is limited to the account market, currency, product, and channel its official source documents. Anything outside that scope is labeled unsupported, never filled in with a guessed rate.</p></section>
  </main>
</Layout>
